{% block user %}Normalized {{ n_obs }} cells to a common library size (target_sum={{ params.get('target_sum') or 'median' }}) and applied log1p transformation; raw counts are preserved in adata.layers["counts_normalized"].{% endblock %}

{% block methods %}Gene expression counts were normalized per cell using sc.pp.normalize_total (target_sum={{ params.get('target_sum') or 'median of raw counts' }}, exclude_highly_expressed={{ params.get('exclude_highly_expressed', False) }}) followed by log(x+1) transformation using sc.pp.log1p, both from Scanpy, following the shifted-logarithm normalization strategy recommended by Luecken and Theis [theis_normalization_2019]. Pre-normalization raw count data were preserved in adata.layers["counts_normalized"] for downstream reference and reproducibility. When target_sum is None, the median total count depth across all cells is used as the scaling target, as recommended to avoid artificial inflation of gene expression in low-complexity libraries.{% endblock %}
